1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,258
EMPLOYEE:

2
00:00:02,258 --> 00:00:03,024
Hello, Picturerep.

3
00:00:03,024 --> 00:00:03,730
Can I help you?

4
00:00:03,730 --> 00:00:03,780
WOMAN:

5
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:04,893
Oh, hi.

6
00:00:04,893 --> 00:00:10,323
I saw your advertisement about copying pictures to disk and I'd like a bit

7
00:00:10,323 --> 00:00:12,650
more information about what you do.

8
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:12,975
EMPLOYEE:

9
00:00:12,975 --> 00:00:13,300
Sure.

10
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:15,250
What would you like to know?

11
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:15,606
WOMAN:

12
00:00:15,606 --> 00:00:20,585
Well, I've got a box full of old family photos that's been up in

13
00:00:20,585 --> 00:00:25,564
the attic for years,some of them must be 50 or 60 years old,

14
00:00:25,564 --> 00:00:29,120
and I'd like to get them converted to digital format.

15
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:29,381
EMPLOYEE:

16
00:00:29,381 --> 00:00:31,210
Sure, we can do that for you.

17
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:31,747
WOMAN:

18
00:00:31,747 --> 00:00:32,283
Right.

19
00:00:32,283 --> 00:00:34,430
And what about size?

20
00:00:34,430 --> 00:00:39,880
The photos are all sorts of sizes – are there any restrictions?

21
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:40,259
EMPLOYEE:

22
00:00:40,259 --> 00:00:45,571
Well the maximum size of photo we can do with our normal service is

23
00:00:45,571 --> 00:00:46,330
30 centimetres.

24
00:00:46,330 --> 00:00:49,486
And each picture must be at least 4 centimetres,

25
00:00:49,486 --> 00:00:51,940
that's the minimum we can cope with.

26
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:52,180
WOMAN:

27
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:53,140
That should be fine.

28
00:00:53,140 --> 00:00:57,468
And some of them are in a frame – should I take them out

29
00:00:57,468 --> 00:00:58,800
before I send them?

30
00:00:58,800 --> 00:00:59,164
EMPLOYEE:

31
00:00:59,164 --> 00:01:01,710
Yes please, we can't copy them otherwise.

32
00:01:01,710 --> 00:01:06,311
And also the photos must all be separate, they mustn't be stuck into an

33
00:01:06,311 --> 00:01:06,640
album.

34
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:07,050
WOMAN:

35
00:01:07,050 --> 00:01:07,460
OK,

36
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:09,100
that's not a problem.

37
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:13,490
So can you give me an idea of how much this will cost?

38
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:17,850
I've got about 360 photos I think.

39
00:01:17,850 --> 00:01:18,391
EMPLOYEE:

40
00:01:18,391 --> 00:01:24,880
We charge ￡195 for 300 to 400 photos for the basic service.

41
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:25,344
WOMAN:

42
00:01:25,344 --> 00:01:25,808
OK.

43
00:01:25,808 --> 00:01:28,590
And does that include the disk?

44
00:01:28,590 --> 00:01:28,961
EMPLOYEE:

45
00:01:28,961 --> 00:01:33,410
Yes, one disk – but you can get extra ones for ￡5 each.

46
00:01:33,410 --> 00:01:33,735
WOMAN:

47
00:01:33,735 --> 00:01:34,386
That's good.

48
00:01:34,386 --> 00:01:38,290
So do I need to pay when I send you the photos?

49
00:01:38,290 --> 00:01:38,657
EMPLOYEE:

50
00:01:38,657 --> 00:01:42,690
No, we won't need anything until we've actually copied the pictures.

51
00:01:42,690 --> 00:01:45,500
Then we'll let you know how much it is,

52
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:49,560
and once we've received the payment, we'll send the parcel off to you.

53
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,635
WOMAN:

54
00:01:51,635 --> 00:01:53,710
Right.

55
00:01:53,710 --> 00:01:54,026
EMPLOYEE:

56
00:01:54,026 --> 00:01:57,500
Is there anything else you'd like to ask about our services?

57
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:57,897
WOMAN:

58
00:01:57,897 --> 00:01:58,293
Yes.

59
00:01:58,293 --> 00:02:03,450
I've roughly sorted out the photos into groups, according to what they're about –

60
00:02:03,450 --> 00:02:08,210
so can you keep them in those groups when you copy them.

61
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:08,528
EMPLOYEE:

62
00:02:08,528 --> 00:02:08,847
Sure.

63
00:02:08,847 --> 00:02:12,349
We'll save each group in a different folder on the disk

64
00:02:12,349 --> 00:02:16,170
and if you like, you can suggest a name for each folder.

65
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:16,618
WOMAN:

66
00:02:16,618 --> 00:02:20,650
So I could have one called ‘Grandparents' for instance?

67
00:02:20,650 --> 00:02:21,390
EMPLOYEE:

68
00:02:21,390 --> 00:02:22,130
Exactly.

69
00:02:22,130 --> 00:02:22,581
WOMAN:

70
00:02:22,581 --> 00:02:26,636
And do you do anything besides scan the photos?

71
00:02:26,636 --> 00:02:29,340
Like, can you make any improvements?

72
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:29,713
EMPLOYEE:

73
00:02:29,713 --> 00:02:33,067
Yes, in the standard service each photo is checked,

74
00:02:33,067 --> 00:02:36,793
and we can sometimes touch up the colour a bit,

75
00:02:36,793 --> 00:02:40,520
or improve the contrast – that can make a big difference.

76
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:40,902
WOMAN:

77
00:02:40,902 --> 00:02:41,283
OK.

78
00:02:41,283 --> 00:02:46,242
And some of the photos are actually quite fragile – they won't get damaged

79
00:02:46,242 --> 00:02:48,150
in the process, will they?

80
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:48,545
EMPLOYEE:

81
00:02:48,545 --> 00:02:52,890
No, if any look particularly fragile, we'd do them by hand.

82
00:02:52,890 --> 00:02:56,230
We do realise how precious these old photos can be.

83
00:02:56,230 --> 00:02:56,750
WOMAN:

84
00:02:56,750 --> 00:02:57,270
Sure.

85
00:02:57,270 --> 00:02:57,610
EMPLOYEE:

86
00:02:57,610 --> 00:03:02,374
And another thing is we can make changes to a photo if you want –

87
00:03:02,374 --> 00:03:06,117
so if you want to remove an object from a photo,

88
00:03:06,117 --> 00:03:09,180
or maybe alter the background, we can do that.

89
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:09,592
WOMAN:

90
00:03:09,592 --> 00:03:10,005
Really?

91
00:03:10,005 --> 00:03:12,480
I might be interested in that.

92
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:15,500
I'll have a look through the photos and see.

93
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:15,947
Oh,

94
00:03:15,947 --> 00:03:22,210
and talking of fixing photos – I've got a few that aren't properly in focus.

95
00:03:22,210 --> 00:03:24,720
Can you do anything to make that better?

96
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:25,092
EMPLOYEE:

97
00:03:25,092 --> 00:03:28,440
No, I'm afraid that's one thing we can't do.

98
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,065
WOMAN:

99
00:03:29,065 --> 00:03:29,690
OK.

100
00:03:29,690 --> 00:03:29,978
EMPLOYEE:

101
00:03:29,978 --> 00:03:31,990
Any other information I can give you?

102
00:03:31,990 --> 00:03:32,453
WOMAN:

103
00:03:32,453 --> 00:03:36,160
Er … oh, how long will it all take?

104
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:36,438
EMPLOYEE:

105
00:03:36,438 --> 00:03:39,220
We aim to get the copying done in ten days.

106
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:39,568
WOMAN:

107
00:03:39,568 --> 00:03:39,917
Fine.

108
00:03:39,917 --> 00:03:43,749
Right, well I'll get the photos packed up in a box

109
00:03:43,749 --> 00:03:45,840
and post them off to you.

110
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:46,235
EMPLOYEE:

111
00:03:46,235 --> 00:03:46,630
Right.

112
00:03:46,630 --> 00:03:49,397
If you've got a strong cardboard box,

113
00:03:49,397 --> 00:03:50,188
that's best.

114
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:54,140
We've found that plastic ones sometimes break in the post.

115
00:03:54,140 --> 00:03:54,752
WOMAN:

116
00:03:54,752 --> 00:03:55,365
OK.

117
00:03:55,365 --> 00:03:58,427
Right, thanks for your help.

118
00:03:58,427 --> 00:03:59,040
Bye.

119
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:00,020
EMPLOYEE:

120
00:04:00,020 --> 00:04:01,000
Bye.
